 {:goal/id :mine-coal
  :goal/priority 10
  :goal/doc
  "dig the nearest exposed coal ore with any pickaxe, or cut stairs down toward it, no deeper than y 40 (the game makes coal densest high up, around y 96, and none below y 0). A spare pickaxe is made while one is still held, from what is carried (sticks, cobblestone, the table): the coal for the ingots is dug at depth after the iron, and race 38477665442 bot Clj_r20 tunnelled for it with its last pickaxe, a wooden one, beside two sticks, a table and 249 cobblestone, until it broke and the run stopped :no-pickaxe (issue #36)"
  :goal/holds {:tag/pickaxes 1}
  :goal/spares {:tag/pickaxes 1}
  :goal/provides {:item/coal 1}
  :goal/act :mine
  :goal/blocks [:coal_ore :deepslate_coal_ore]
  :goal/depth 40
  :goal/done? :provided?}
 {:goal/id :mine-iron
  :goal/priority 10
  :goal/doc
  "dig the nearest exposed iron ore with a stone pickaxe, or cut stairs down toward it and tunnel at y 16, where the game makes iron densest. A spare pickaxe is made before more ore is dug, gathering the wood when a walk to a trunk or stairs up to one can be started, so the last one is not worn out at the bottom. A walk back up the dug shaft is not that: it reaches the sky, not a tree. Four sticks are kept too, two more pickaxes' handles, gathered up at the trees before the descent: the stairs down, the tunnels and the climb out for the water dig some 390 blocks, three stone pickaxes' worth, and race 38477665442 bots Clj_r23 and Clj_r06 left the forest with three logs, made three pickaxes and broke the last on the climb (issue #39)"
  :goal/holds {:item/stone_pickaxe 1}
  :goal/spares {:item/stone_pickaxe 1 :item/stick 4}
  :goal/provides {:item/raw_iron 1}
  :goal/act :mine
  :goal/blocks [:iron_ore :deepslate_iron_ore]
  :goal/depth 16
  :goal/done? :provided?}
